      },
      "worked": "Basketball heights in ascending order (cm): $194,\\ 195,\\ \\underline{197},\\ 200,\\ 201$.\n\nThere are five values, so the third value is the middle value. The basketball players’ median height is $197\\,\\text{cm}$.\n\nGymnast heights in ascending order (cm): $146,\\ 152,\\ \\underline{154},\\ \\underline{158},\\ 158,\\ 160$.\n\nThere are six values, so find the mean of the third and fourth values.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Gymnast median}&=\\frac{154+158}{2}\\,\\text{cm}\\\\\\text{Gymnast median}&=156\\,\\text{cm}\\end{align*}$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Difference}&=(197-156)\\,\\text{cm}\\\\\\text{Difference}&=41\\,\\text{cm}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe basketball players’ median height is $41\\,\\text{cm}$ greater. Greater height can give an advantage when reaching the basket or taking rebounds. This is a possible reason for the taller basketball players in these samples.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
